1. emptyDir
Created when a Pod starts.
Deleted when the Pod is deleted.
Shared between all containers in the Pod.

Directly created using deployment file 
volumes:
- name: cache-volume
  emptyDir: {}

containers:
- name: app
  volumeMounts:
  - mountPath: /cache
    name: cache-volume

Lifecycle
Pod Starts
      │
emptyDir Created
      │
Containers Share Data
      │
Pod Deleted
      │
Data Deleted
--------------------------------------------------------

2. hostPath

Uses a directory from the Kubernetes node.

volumes:
- name: host-storage
  hostPath:
    path: /data/logs
----------------------------------------------------------

3. PersistentVolume (PV)

A PersistentVolume (PV) is storage created by the cluster administrator or dynamically by a StorageClass.

Lifecycle
Application
     │
PVC
     │
PV
     │
AWS EBS

------------------------------------------


4. PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC)

A PVC is a request for storage by a Pod.

Example

kind: PersistentVolumeClaim

spec:
  accessModes:
  - ReadWriteOnce

  resources:
    requests:
      storage: 10Gi

The Pod mounts the PVC instead of directly using the PV.
  ----------------------------------------------------------
  StorageClass

StorageClass dynamically creates PersistentVolumes.

Without StorageClass
Admin creates PV
       │
PVC uses PV

With StorageClass
PVC Created
      │
StorageClass
      │
Automatically Creates PV

Example
kind: StorageClass
provisioner: ebs.csi.aws.com
parameters:
  type: gp3
  ------------------------------------------------------

 6. ConfigMap Volume

Stores non-sensitive configuration files.

Example

volumes:
- name: config-volume
  configMap:
    name: app-config

Mounted as

/etc/config
    |
    |-- application.properties

Use Cases

application.properties
nginx.conf
config.yaml
  ---------------------------------------------------
7. Secret Volume

Stores sensitive data.

Example

volumes:
- name: secret-volume
  secret:
    secretName: db-secret

Mounted as

/etc/secret

username
password

Use Cases

Database password
API key
TLS certificates
  ----------------------------------------
8. NFS Volume

Mounts a shared Network File System.

NFS Server
     │
-----------------------
| Node1  Node2  Node3 |
-----------------------
     │
Shared Storage

Example

volumes:
- name: nfs-volume
  nfs:
    server: 10.10.10.20
    path: /shared

Use Cases

Shared storage
Multiple Pods reading/writing the same data
